{"id":"exam-day","title":"Exam day: managing time and nerves","subject":"Study skills","label":"Study skills","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":153,"duration":152.78,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":459,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Exam day","start":0,"end":11.115},{"id":"explain","title":"Night and morning","start":11.115,"end":31.825},{"id":"explain2","title":"Hall and nerves","start":31.825,"end":69.665},{"id":"example","title":"Time per mark","start":69.665,"end":84.865},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":84.865,"end":94.635},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":94.635,"end":102.285},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":102.285,"end":130.745},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":130.745,"end":152.78}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":5.69,"text":"Have you ever known your work, then lost it all when the exam paper landed? I'm Kora.","w":[0.52,0.66,0.82,1.04,1.26,1.44,2.1,2.34,2.7,2.94,3.14,3.28,3.44,3.8,4.12,5.14,5.32]},{"s":0,"a":5.99,"b":10.69,"text":"Today we'll plan exam day so your time and your nerves both work for you, not against you.","w":[6,6.5,6.7,6.96,7.34,7.56,7.72,7.9,8.28,8.4,8.56,8.9,9.14,9.34,9.46,9.98,10.16,10.48]},{"s":1,"a":11.54,"b":15.96,"text":"Start the night before. Pack everything you need, then stop revising early.","w":[11.66,11.96,12.08,12.28,13,13.36,13.72,13.86,14.52,14.84,15.16,15.66]},{"s":1,"a":16.26,"b":20,"text":"Check your exam card, pens, and water, and put them by the door.","w":[16.3,16.52,16.68,17.04,17.54,18,18.16,18.94,19.1,19.26,19.42,19.58,19.68]},{"s":1,"a":20.3,"b":23.35,"text":"Sleep matters, because sleep is when memory settles.","w":[20.42,20.84,21.5,21.82,22.18,22.28,22.44,22.84]},{"s":1,"a":23.65,"b":28.96,"text":"In the morning, eat something, arrive early, and avoid panicked last minute talk.","w":[23.72,23.82,23.94,24.74,24.94,25.84,26.3,27.08,27.2,27.58,28,28.34,28.58]},{"s":1,"a":29.26,"b":31.4,"text":"Give yourself quiet time before you enter.","w":[29.3,29.48,29.9,30.26,30.58,30.88,31.06]},{"s":2,"a":32.25,"b":36.19,"text":"In the hall, read the instructions and check how many questions to answer.","w":[32.3,32.42,32.54,33.34,33.58,33.7,34.56,34.72,34.96,35.08,35.28,35.72,35.88]},{"s":2,"a":36.49,"b":37.78,"text":"Check the clock as you start.","w":[36.52,36.76,36.88,37.24,37.34,37.5]},{"s":2,"a":38.08,"b":40.63,"text":"Work out time per mark or per question.","w":[38.14,38.42,38.6,38.96,39.2,39.78,39.94,40.2]},{"s":2,"a":40.93,"b":45.15,"text":"Do a first pass: answer what you know, mark the hard ones, then come back.","w":[40.93,41.1,41.2,41.52,42.38,42.66,42.82,42.94,43.48,43.76,43.88,44.16,44.5,44.72,44.92]},{"s":2,"a":45.45,"b":50.55,"text":"Never leave a multiple choice question blank unless marks are deducted for wrong answers.","w":[45.56,45.9,46.16,46.26,46.74,47.06,47.5,48.2,48.56,48.92,49.04,49.54,49.7,50.04]},{"s":2,"a":50.85,"b":53.49,"text":"If there is no penalty, always give an answer.","w":[50.92,51.02,51.2,51.34,51.54,52.52,52.9,53.06,53.18]},{"s":2,"a":53.79,"b":54.76,"text":"Show your working.","w":[53.92,54.16,54.34]},{"s":2,"a":55.06,"b":57.3,"text":"Some nerves are normal and can sharpen you.","w":[55.16,55.4,55.72,55.88,56.4,56.54,56.74,57.1]},{"s":2,"a":57.6,"b":60.08,"text":"If your mind goes blank, put the pen down.","w":[57.66,57.76,57.96,58.28,58.6,59.22,59.38,59.48,59.72]},{"s":2,"a":60.38,"b":64.06,"text":"Breathe in slowly for four counts and out for six, a few times.","w":[60.46,60.8,60.96,61.38,61.6,61.88,62.36,62.54,62.72,62.9,63.34,63.42,63.6]},{"s":2,"a":64.36,"b":66.74,"text":"Slow breathing tells your body you are safe.","w":[64.48,64.82,65.28,65.58,65.76,66.1,66.28,66.48]},{"s":2,"a":67.04,"b":69.24,"text":"Then start with any question you can do.","w":[67.12,67.38,67.66,68.02,68.26,68.7,68.84,69]},{"s":3,"a":70.09,"b":72.97,"text":"Say you have a two hour paper worth one hundred marks.","w":[70.18,70.44,70.62,70.8,70.92,71.12,71.4,71.76,72.14,72.3,72.6]},{"s":3,"a":73.27,"b":76.98,"text":"Two hours is one hundred and twenty minutes. Keep ten back for checking.","w":[73.28,73.5,73.96,74.2,74.38,74.7,74.84,75.12,75.78,76.02,76.24,76.46,76.62]},{"s":3,"a":77.28,"b":81.6,"text":"That leaves one hundred and ten minutes, so a little over one minute per mark.","w":[77.3,77.52,77.94,78.1,78.44,78.56,78.8,79.64,79.84,79.94,80.28,80.62,80.78,81.06,81.28]},{"s":3,"a":81.9,"b":84.44,"text":"So a ten mark question gets about eleven minutes.","w":[81.98,82.16,82.26,82.52,82.76,83.18,83.38,83.66,84]},{"s":4,"a":85.29,"b":88.43,"text":"Quick check. A ninety minute paper has sixty marks.","w":[85.34,85.6,86.28,86.4,86.72,86.98,87.34,87.56,87.96]},{"s":4,"a":88.73,"b":91.59,"text":"About how long should you spend on a six mark question?","w":[88.8,89.1,89.36,89.68,89.88,90.02,90.4,90.52,90.64,90.92,91.16]},{"s":4,"a":92.04,"b":94.21,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[92.04,92.36,92.64,92.78,93.06,93.66,93.84]},{"s":5,"a":95.06,"b":101.86,"text":"About nine minutes at most. Ninety minutes over sixty marks is one and a half minutes per mark, and that times six is nine.","w":[95.14,95.44,95.7,96.02,96.14,96.92,97.22,97.48,97.7,98.02,98.4,98.64,98.78,98.88,98.98,99.26,99.54,99.7,100.34,100.46,100.68,101.06,101.4,101.56]},{"s":6,"a":102.71,"b":107.72,"text":"One common mistake is spending too long on one hard question. Mark it and move on.","w":[102.86,103.04,103.38,103.84,103.94,104.36,104.62,105.1,105.38,105.58,105.86,106.68,106.96,107.12,107.24,107.56]},{"s":6,"a":108.02,"b":110.23,"text":"That protects marks you can already earn.","w":[108.08,108.32,108.78,109.08,109.22,109.46,109.9]},{"s":6,"a":110.53,"b":117.6,"text":"Another is not reading the command word in the question, like explain or compare, so you answer the wrong way. Read it twice.","w":[110.6,111.04,111.18,111.46,111.76,111.88,112.3,112.52,112.6,112.72,113.36,113.58,114.04,114.14,115.16,115.36,115.58,115.86,115.98,116.24,116.74,116.94,117.08]},{"s":6,"a":117.9,"b":120.61,"text":"The command word tells you what kind of answer is needed.","w":[117.9,118.04,118.44,118.72,119,119.18,119.4,119.62,119.78,120.12,120.24]},{"s":6,"a":120.91,"b":126.48,"text":"A third is changing right answers out of panic without a reason. Only change if you find a real error.","w":[120.96,121.08,121.4,121.54,122.02,122.32,122.72,122.84,122.98,123.36,123.68,123.74,124.62,124.9,125.26,125.36,125.52,125.78,125.86,126.2]},{"s":6,"a":126.78,"b":130.32,"text":"Trust your first careful answer unless you see a clear mistake.","w":[126.8,127.12,127.38,127.7,128.12,128.78,129.1,129.26,129.44,129.56,129.84]},{"s":7,"a":131.17,"b":135.09,"text":"Recap. Work out your time per mark, and keep ten minutes to check.","w":[131.22,132.16,132.42,132.56,132.74,133.04,133.26,133.84,133.96,134.24,134.48,134.78,134.92]},{"s":7,"a":135.39,"b":138.23,"text":"Do a first pass, and come back to the hard ones.","w":[135.42,135.62,135.72,136.02,136.7,136.86,137.08,137.34,137.48,137.6,137.92]},{"s":7,"a":138.53,"b":142.55,"text":"Nerves are normal. Breathe in for four and out for six if you blank.","w":[138.6,139,139.14,139.82,140.22,140.4,140.64,140.98,141.18,141.36,141.58,141.92,142.02,142.18]},{"s":7,"a":142.85,"b":148.11,"text":"Top tip: if a question steals your time, mark it and return only when the easier marks are safe.","w":[142.86,143.16,143.8,143.92,144,144.42,144.7,144.86,145.68,145.94,146.08,146.2,146.66,146.88,147.04,147.18,147.48,147.74,147.86]},{"s":7,"a":148.41,"b":152.18,"text":"Knowzone is here whenever you want to practise again. You can do this.","w":[148.48,148.98,149.1,149.38,149.72,149.86,150.04,150.16,150.58,151.3,151.46,151.62,151.78]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Exam day","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Know your work? Keep it when paper lands"},{"at":5.89,"kind":"text","text":"Plan exam day: time and nerves work for you"}]},{"at":11.29,"heading":"Night and morning","items":[{"at":11.44,"kind":"text","text":"Night before: pack, stop revising early"},{"at":16.16,"kind":"text","text":"Exam card, pens, water by the door"},{"at":20.2,"kind":"term","text":"Sleep","detail":"Memory settles during sleep"},{"at":23.55,"kind":"text","text":"Morning: eat, arrive early, avoid panic talk"},{"at":29.16,"kind":"text","text":"Quiet time before you enter"}]},{"at":32,"heading":"In the hall","items":[{"at":32.15,"kind":"text","text":"Read instructions; check question count"},{"at":36.39,"kind":"text","text":"Check the clock as you start"},{"at":37.98,"kind":"formula","text":"Time per mark = total time ÷ marks"},{"at":40.83,"kind":"text","text":"First pass: do known, mark hard, return"},{"at":45.35,"kind":"text","text":"MCQ: leave blank only if wrong answers penalised"}]},{"at":53.54,"heading":"Nerves and blanking","items":[{"at":53.69,"kind":"text","text":"Show your working"},{"at":54.96,"kind":"text","text":"Some nerves are normal; can sharpen you"},{"at":57.5,"kind":"text","text":"Mind blank: pen down; breathe 4 in, 6 out"},{"at":64.26,"kind":"term","text":"Slow breathing","detail":"Tells your body you are safe"},{"at":66.94,"kind":"text","text":"Then start with any question you can do"}]},{"at":69.84,"heading":"Time per mark","items":[{"at":69.99,"kind":"formula","text":"2 h paper; 100 marks"},{"at":73.17,"kind":"formula","text":"2 h = 120 min; keep 10 min"},{"at":77.18,"kind":"formula","text":"110 min ÷ 100 marks = 1.1 min/mark"},{"at":81.8,"kind":"step","text":"10 marks → 11 min"}]},{"at":84.86,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":84.86,"kind":"question","text":"A 90-minute paper has 60 marks. About how long should you spend on a 6-mark question?"}]},{"at":94.81,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":94.96,"kind":"formula","text":"90 min ÷ 60 marks = 1.5 min/mark"},{"at":94.96,"kind":"formula","text":"1.5 × 6 = 9 min"}]},{"at":102.46,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":102.61,"kind":"wrong","text":"Spend too long on one hard question"},{"at":107.92,"kind":"text","text":"Protects marks you can already earn"},{"at":110.43,"kind":"wrong","text":"Ignore command word: explain or compare"},{"at":117.8,"kind":"term","text":"Command word","detail":"Tells you what kind of answer is needed"},{"at":120.81,"kind":"wrong","text":"Change right answers out of panic"}]},{"at":130.92,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":131.07,"kind":"text","text":"Work out time per mark; keep 10 min to check"},{"at":135.29,"kind":"text","text":"First pass; return to hard ones"},{"at":138.43,"kind":"text","text":"Nerves normal; breathe 4 in, 6 out if blank"},{"at":142.75,"kind":"tip","text":"If a question steals your time, mark it and return when easier marks are safe."},{"at":148.31,"kind":"text","text":"Knowzone: practise again. You can do this."}]}],"check":{"at":94.46,"seconds":10,"question":"A 90-minute paper has 60 marks. About how long should you spend on a 6-mark question?","answer":"About 9 minutes: 90 ÷ 60 = 1.5 min per mark; 1.5 × 6 = 9 min."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}